# Land

When the user asks to land, merge, or 合入 a pull request, treat that as a closeout gate. Identify the target PR and its HEAD SHA. Merge only after both gates below succeed on that exact SHA.

## 1. Autoreview

If an `autoreview` skill is available (project `.agents/skills/autoreview` or `.claude/skills/autoreview`, or global `~/.agents` / `~/.claude`), read it and run it against the PR/branch being landed, using the PR base (`--mode branch --base origin/<base>`). Skip this gate only when the skill is absent; say so.

A clean helper exit with no accepted/actionable findings is required. Report remaining findings and stop. Do not merge. If review requires code changes, stop the land, report them, and wait for a new HEAD plus a fresh CI run.

## 2. CI

Every check run on the PR HEAD must be `completed` and `success`. Query `gh pr checks` and the commit check-runs API for that SHA. Duplicate `push` and `pull_request` jobs both count. Pending, queued, failed, cancelled, or timed-out checks block land. Combined Status API `pending` with an empty status list is not evidence of failure when check-runs are green.

## Merge

Draft, conflicted, or non-mergeable PRs stay unmerged. Use `gh pr merge` with the repository default method. Do not bypass checks.
